.Dd November 24, 2026
.Dt AETERNUM-INSTALLER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm aeternum-installer
.Nd install Aeternum Security OS on a disk
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm install-aeternum
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility copies the running live system to a disk of the machine, and makes
that disk bootable in UEFI mode.
It must be run as root.
.Nm install-aeternum
is the desktop launcher: it opens a terminal and runs
.Nm
through
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Pp
The utility lists the disks reported by
.Xr sysctl 8
.Va kern.disks ,
excluding optical drives and the boot medium, and asks for the name of the
disk to use.
It then asks for the word
.Li INSTALLA
as confirmation.
.Pp
.Sy All data on the selected disk is destroyed .
.Pp
The installation proceeds in these steps:
.Bl -enum
.It
The disk is given a GPT scheme with a 260 MB EFI partition (label
.Li aeternum-efi )
and a UFS partition with soft updates using the rest of the disk (label
.Li aeternum-root ) ,
using
.Xr gpart 8 ,
.Xr newfs_msdos 8
and
.Xr newfs 8 .
.It
The live system is copied to the new root with
.Xr tar 1 ,
through a read-only
.Xr nullfs 5
mount of
.Pa / .
.It
.Pa /etc/fstab ,
.Pa /boot/loader.conf
and
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
are written for the installed system, and the live-only files are removed.
.It
.Pa /boot/loader.efi
is copied to
.Pa EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI
on the EFI partition.
.El
.Pp
The installed system has the user
.Li admin
with the password
.Li admin .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/local/sbin/aeternum-installer
The installer.
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/install-aeternum
The desktop launcher.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr gpart 8 ,
.Xr newfs 8 ,
.Xr newfs_msdos 8 ,
.Xr aeternum 7
.Sh BUGS
UEFI only.
The installer has not yet been tested on physical hardware.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Zef Lleshaj
